# =============================================================================
# Marketing video projects (marketing/videos/*)
# =============================================================================
# Regenerable build/tool output. Rebuild with each project's own package.json
# scripts (npm run dev / check / render). Applies to every project under
# marketing/videos/, so a new one is safe by default. See marketing/videos/README.md.
marketing/videos/*/out/
marketing/videos/*/renders/
marketing/videos/*/snapshots/
marketing/videos/*/.thumbnails/
marketing/videos/*/.hyperframes/
marketing/videos/*/agent/skills/
marketing/videos/*/.agents/skills/

# Third-party reference footage and everything derived from it (clips, extracted
# frames, contact sheets, audio, downloader metadata). Re-downloadable from the
# source URL; too large and not ours to distribute. The small hand-made analysis
# that lives beside it — scenes.json, scenes_raw.txt, subtitles, key frames — IS
# tracked, since that is our own work.
marketing/videos/*/reference/clips/
marketing/videos/*/reference/frames/
marketing/videos/*/reference/sheets/
marketing/videos/*/reference/*.mp4
marketing/videos/*/reference/*.mp3
marketing/videos/*/reference/*.webp
marketing/videos/*/reference/*.info.json

# =============================================================================
# AI-agent tooling (repo root)
# =============================================================================
# Vendored skill packages, regenerated from the tracked skills-lock.json.
# .claude/skills/ are OS symlinks into .agents/skills/ — never git-add them:
# this checkout has core.symlinks=false, so git would flatten each one into a
# text file containing its absolute target path.
/.agents/skills/
/.claude/skills/
# Per-machine runtime state (a PID + process start time), not shareable.
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
